*> PLB-C097 sort-file-open: SORT or MERGE USING or GIVING a file that
*> an OPEN before it left open.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SORTOPEN.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO "in.dat" ORGANIZATION LINE SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
    SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "out.dat" ORGANIZATION LINE SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
    SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN TO "work".
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  IN-FILE.
01  IN-REC              PIC X(10).
FD  OUT-FILE.
01  OUT-REC             PIC X(10).
SD  SORT-FILE.
01  SORT-REC            PIC X(10).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-FS               PIC XX.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    *> Reported: the USING file, and the GIVING file in the next
    *> sentence.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    SORT SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-REC USING IN-FILE
        GIVING OUT-FILE
    OPEN OUTPUT OUT-FILE.
    SORT SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-REC USING IN-FILE
        GIVING OUT-FILE.
    *> Not reported: closed first, and a PERFORM between.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    CLOSE IN-FILE
    SORT SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-REC USING IN-FILE
        GIVING OUT-FILE
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    PERFORM CLOSE-IN
    SORT SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-REC USING IN-FILE
        GIVING OUT-FILE
    STOP RUN.
CLOSE-IN.
    CLOSE IN-FILE.
